{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116212",
      "title": "Working with RxJS Operators",
      "lectureOrder": 211,
      "videoOrder": 202,
      "sourceHash": "6b948aa606ed517b8d03f07484c09df89a3094d815e77ed4e802844422d5d514",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 2.7,
          "en": "So, in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "we created an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "based on an interval which fires every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "And this could be a valid use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "You might be building an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.12,
          "en": "where something should happen every couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.12,
          "end": 22.05,
          "en": "For example, you might wanna send an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.05,
          "end": 25.299,
          "en": "and fetch data every X seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.299,
          "end": 30.299,
          "en": "or you might want to update some UI element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 35.39,
          "en": "for an animation or something like that every X seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 39.36,
          "en": "In such scenarios, you could use this interval function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.36,
          "end": 43.65,
          "en": "to handle these use cases with an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.65,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "You don't have to, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "There always also are alternative ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 52.2,
          "en": "of implementing such features, but you could.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.2,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "Now, this interval function here is of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 59.1,
          "en": "not the only function you can use to create an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.1,
          "end": 62.13,
          "en": "Instead, if you take a look at the official documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.13,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "you'll find plenty of functions you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 67.47,
          "en": "when working with RxJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 72.47,
          "en": "though not all of these functions will create observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "Instead, indeed, most of these functions operate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "on existing observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "and allow you to manipulate them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "or their values to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 88.14,
          "en": "Because RxJS also has this concept of operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.14,
          "end": 91.59,
          "en": "which you can use when dealing with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.59,
          "end": 94.624,
          "en": "which are in the end functions you can pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.624,
          "end": 99.624,
          "en": "into your observable data stream to perform transformations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 101.61,
          "en": "or any other kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.61,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "of operation on those observable values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "And I'll show you an example here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 110.00999999999999,
          "en": "for this interval observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.00999999999999,
          "end": 113.75999999999999,
          "en": "You can add operators to this observable pipeline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "by calling the pipe method before you subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "And indeed, you need at least one subscriber",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "to kick off the observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 125.97,
          "en": "If you do not subscribe at least once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "there will be no values being emitted here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 130.743,
          "en": "That's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "But with that, I'm calling pipe here before I'm subscribing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "And pipe then allows you to add some operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 143.497,
          "en": "some RxJS operators to this pipeline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.497,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "And you'll find these operator functions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 148.56,
          "en": "in the official documentation as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "Of course, not just in the reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "but also if you go to the dedicated operators page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 156.31799999999998,
          "en": "where you can learn all about them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.31799999999998,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "Though, as I mentioned before, it in the end depends on you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "the team you work in and your personal preferences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "how deep you want to dive into RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 171.72,
          "en": "It's a feature you can use in your Angular apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.72,
          "end": 175.26,
          "en": "but not a feature you have to use too much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 177.72,
          "en": "Nonetheless, here to get started with operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.72,
          "end": 180.06,
          "en": "I'll add the map operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "which therefore must be imported from RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 186.963,
          "en": "So the map function is imported here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 192.39,
          "en": "This function is then called here as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "for this pipe function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 197.853,
          "en": "and that then adds it as an operator to this pipeline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 202.05,
          "en": "Now if we take a look at the official reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 204.733,
          "en": "and we search for this map function there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.733,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "we can see that this is an operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "which in the end converts a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "that is emitted by an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 215.97,
          "en": "So it in the end is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.97,
          "end": 218.34,
          "en": "that takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.34,
          "end": 222.18,
          "en": "And that function will then be executed on every value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 224.16,
          "en": "that's emitted by the observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.16,
          "end": 226.44,
          "en": "and it's then the function result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.44,
          "end": 228.663,
          "en": "that will be passed to the subscribers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "So here we can pass a function to map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 234.63,
          "en": "and we'll get the value that's emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.63,
          "end": 237.06,
          "en": "by this observable on which we call map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.06,
          "end": 240.788,
          "en": "In the end, we'll get that as an input here as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.788,
          "end": 245.16,
          "en": "and we then must return the updated value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "Now, since interval gives us a value of type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 251.958,
          "en": "we can, for example, multiply it with two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.958,
          "end": 255.12,
          "en": "and the subscriber will then get the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.12,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "of this operator here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 260.04,
          "en": "So the doubled number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.04,
          "end": 263.35,
          "en": "And we could add multiple operators here if we wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.577,
          "end": 268.097,
          "en": "to perform multiple operations, not just map operations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.097,
          "end": 269.49,
          "en": "but any kind of operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.49,
          "end": 272.454,
          "en": "Here, however it is just map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.454,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "With that, if we do that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 278.235,
          "en": "you'll see we still got some numbers being locked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.235,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "but now we got double the number than before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 285.39,
          "en": "So two instead of one, four instead of two, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.39,
          "end": 289.5,
          "en": "Because we added this map operator here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.5,
          "end": 294.5,
          "en": "And operators indeed are one of the key RX features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.11,
          "end": 299.25,
          "en": "And also one important difference between observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.25,
          "end": 303.132,
          "en": "and signals, though I'll get back to that in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.132,
          "end": 306.27,
          "en": "But operators are an important feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 306.27,
          "end": 310.29,
          "en": "and you'll see me use some operators at least from time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 310.29,
          "end": 312.663,
          "en": "to time throughout the rest of this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.57,
          "end": 314.97,
          "en": "though all then always explain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.97,
          "end": 318.112,
          "en": "why I'm using a certain operator and what it'll do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 318.112,
          "end": 321.42,
          "en": "It's just important for now to be aware of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 324.45,
          "en": "that with RxJS and these observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.45,
          "end": 326.31,
          "en": "you can add these operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.31,
          "end": 330.21,
          "en": "that will then operate on the values that are emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.21,
          "end": 332.493,
          "en": "and managed by the observable.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
